{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact sales-design draft8 57c9a984e22e8c708c65a44462b05d62b4d648f4 / tree7f67aed37b99d442c0fed7849ea5f6fddc7e4f8a, primaryf122a162, notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md. Full670-line primary read first in full. The earlier substantive publication protocol and bid-capacity findings are resolved. Two small remaining calendar corrections prevent approval.\n\nF3 core resolved: the send's result is now admission only, with applied/refused/superseded distinguished from the later push/public receipt. report-receipt-check is explicitly an attributed member statement and never native Destination confirmation; the actual completion protocol is deferred. This matches the landed Result construction/verification and lending publication boundary. Preserve this distinction.\n\nF3 remaining, medium — Make the calendar's state declaration match its result effects (6.2 lines556–557,6.3 lines573–574). The text says the admission clause changes the post to refused on refusal, but post.states lists planned/drafted/approved/publishing/admitted/retired and omits refused. A declared effect cannot select an undeclared state. Add the refusal state and choose an explicit mapping for the superseded admission result, or keep a declared request-outcome value separate from post.state. Align the interaction, definitions and log; do not reintroduce 'published' as a native confirmation. This is a local enum/effect correction, not a new completion protocol.\n\nF5 bid resolved: one import and50 requirements per bid, each whole queried representation≤2KiB UTF-8 with conservative component limits and write-time refusals, give a stated total≤102400bytes before bounded envelope overhead, below half of the256KiB complete-source limit. The sealed rendering≤64KiB matches publish-file, and the50-row limit also stays below the64-element value-list ceiling for an assembly's answer list. Replacement/deferred larger data and the51-row/oversized-answer witness are explicit. This is a design budget still to be enforced by the eventual definitions; no measured runtime acceptance is inferred.\n\nF5 remaining, medium — Bound the calendar's complete active post source too (6.2/6.3,7,C1). The new per-post text limit is32KiB but there is no aggregate post/count/representation limit for its routed calendar carousel. The described month can contain nine drafted posts at that allowed limit: their text alone is294912bytes, already above the262144-byte ItemQuery/projection limit before briefs, titles, refs and metadata. The complete read refuses before routing can select the owner's posts, even if fewer than100 rows exist. Apply an explicit conservative aggregate active-post/count and full-row byte policy, or smaller text maxima, to keep that complete source inside the existing budget; refuse later draft growth before it strands the calendar. A small bounded first version is sufficient. Changing projected aliases alone does not bypass the preceding native ItemQuery payload limit. Keep the first version within current limits rather than implying a pagination feature.\n\nF1, F2 and F4 remain resolved: fixed domain acts/assigned signer guards and shared review action; separate uniquely guarded approval openings with current-import/all-row/current-approval/immutable-assembly checks; notice/index writes rather than deletion. The narrower buyer/custody/hosted-agent/integration boundaries remain correct.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: bounded package definitions and existing native views/scopes/publication admission support the proposed processes. The main protocol gap is now honestly deferred. Complete-source budgets apply to the calendar as well as the bid, and the declared post states must admit the result effects the note describes.\n\nSecurity conclusion: agent drafts, expert supply, team review, management seal, native admission and member-reported external checks now retain separate authority and attribution. A member's check is not upgraded into independent destination-confirmed state. Buyer exclusion and references without private custody remain explicit.\n\nSimplification conclusion: keep the resolved admission/report boundary and bid bounds. One calendar source bound and a consistent refusal/supersession state mapping finish the remaining corrections; no new native form, completion protocol, query paging or larger limit is requested. C1-C4 remain deferred behind plan033; this note commissions no implementation.\n\nValidation: final primary and changed sections checked, sole Markdown change from Main2127, all10 local links/heading fragments resolve, whitespace clean. SHA256e4605343bf75a48c9d61143d05f5639145a7c590edc158ff590ce72928a49b16. Native prepare binds7f569087/28988cd9/reportf122a162 at this exact head. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-sales-design-jne3y8sq retains primary/diff/validation; byte counterexamples are arithmetic, not a runtime test run. Prior unchanged contract/judge/Result/projection/Destination source checks reused. No source/test edits, tests/gate rerun, package install, provider/publication/deployment action.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f122a1621e6d99122df06a74ac3c392d1f4923d7","binding":"assigned","head":"57c9a984e22e8c708c65a44462b05d62b4d648f4","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:572660ef0f6a42ce60ef352a8711b4084ed9aac5\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:28988cd98dfb9eddaadb8934b253cc352c17814f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:572660ef0f6a42ce60ef352a8711b4084ed9aac5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}